Subject: prevent rotation of geom_tippoint shapes in circular tree
Message-ID: <FbJ1EreLGyY.Dcmlz25xAwAJ@bioc-ggtree.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/bioc-ggtree/c/FbJ1EreLGyY/m/Dcmlz25xAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello everyone,
Not sure if this has been asked before, but I would very much like to know if it is possible to sort of "lock" the tip point shape relative to the center of the tree when using a circular layout?

As of now, this is what it looks like:

```
test <- rtree(7)

metadata <- data.frame(sample = c("t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"),
                       var = c("A", "A", "B", "A", "B","B","B"))

ggtree(test,
       layout = "circular") %<+% metadata +
  geom_tippoint(aes(shape = var),
                size = 3)
```

However, I would like the triangles to be locked in the same position relative to the center, so that all of the triangles are pointing inwards rather than being rotated like above. Any way of doing this?

